      <p class="route-card__why">High risk.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Lenders.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>None.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Debt.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Test first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> run the five-step test, get three paying customers and only then decide on funding or further study.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep personal savings separate and protected.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Customers and partners pay for solved problems. They judge you by reliability, price and whether you do what you promised.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is getting one real payment for a real offer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA entrepreneurship: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft reports, summaries and outreach. Routine output becomes common quickly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, relationships and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for drafts; later, own the decisions and the people.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general MBA entrepreneurship path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Alternative</th>
          <th>Why it can beat it</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Job first, venture later</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Income and learning</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Slower</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Incubator programme</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Support and network</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Competitive</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Freelance first</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Low cost test</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Different from a product</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="learn">How to learn MBA entrepreneurship cheaply, and what proof counts</h2>

  <p>
    MBA entrepreneurship is learned by doing real work, so the cheapest route is also the best. A paid course is worth it only when it gives feedback and finished work that you cannot get free.
  </p>
  <h3>Free and low-cost routes first</h3>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Free YouTube lessons and public company reports.</li>
    <li>Free NPTEL and SWAYAM management and statistics courses.</li>
    <li>Free spreadsheet practice with public data.</li>
    <li>A professional in the role who reviews your sample.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>How to judge a paid course</h3>
  <p>
    Judge each course, not the platform. Ask what you will build, who reviews it, which role graduates reached, how current the material is and what the refund terms are, in writing.
  </p>
  <h3>Your week, and a first small test</h3>
  <p>
    A starting plan is about ten hours a week: three of lessons and seven of practice on one project. Do not pay for an expensive programme before this habit holds.
  </p>
  <p>
    In four weeks, interview ten people about one problem and try to get one paying customer.
  </p>
  <h3>Building a high-income skill portfolio beside the credential</h3>
  <p>
    A degree has a place, and the weak spot is relying on it alone. A skill mix of one core skill, a second skill, communication, a niche and a clear offer builds a high-income skill portfolio, and a niche service can bring an earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

  <h2 id="startroutes">Five routes in the startup world</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Route</th>
