          <th>Risk</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Found a venture</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Build and sell your own product or service</td>
          <td data-label="Risk">Cash and time</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Join early-stage as a generalist</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Own growth, operations or sales</td>
          <td data-label="Risk">Pay and stability</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Join a family business</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Modernise or expand it</td>
          <td data-label="Risk">Roles and decisions are shared</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Work in venture or incubator support</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Evaluate and support founders</td>
          <td data-label="Risk">Competitive and few openings</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Corporate innovation roles</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Build new lines inside a firm</td>
          <td data-label="Risk">Slow decisions</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="test">A low-cost venture test before you borrow</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Step</th>
          <th>What to do</th>
          <th>Pass if</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Problem</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Interview ten people who have it</td>
          <td data-label="Pass if">At least five describe it unprompted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Offer</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Describe the solution in two lines and a price</td>
          <td data-label="Pass if">Some say they would pay</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Sell</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Try to get three paying customers</td>
          <td data-label="Pass if">Three real payments or signed commitments</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Unit view</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Write cost and price for one unit</td>
          <td data-label="Pass if">Positive margin on paper</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Runway</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Calculate months you can survive</td>
          <td data-label="Pass if">At least twelve months of personal costs covered</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="numbers">Money numbers every founder should know</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Number</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
          <th>Trap</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Number"><strong>Cost to get a customer</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Meaning">Money spent to win one</td>
          <td data-label="Trap">Counting only ad spend</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Number"><strong>Margin</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Meaning">Price minus cost for each sale</td>
          <td data-label="Trap">Forgetting your own time</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Number"><strong>Runway</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Meaning">Months of cash left</td>
          <td data-label="Trap">Planning on the best case</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Number"><strong>Repeat rate</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Meaning">Share of customers who return</td>
          <td data-label="Trap">Confusing signups with buyers</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    As a rule of thumb, many families plan about 10 percent of income on education and up to 20 percent with caution. This is an illustration, not a real fee, so test a venture before treating a costly programme as the way in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>

  <p>
    As a rule of thumb and not a research finding, keep a degree or course fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 8 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 80,000 for the main course, and a fifth is Rs 1.6 lakh as a serious caution. The rest can fund a laptop, practice time and a reserve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Test the field with free courses and one finished project before paying for a long programme. Do not borrow heavily for a course whose graduates cannot show placement in a specific role.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol for this career</h2>

  <p>
    Test the choice with <strong>The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</strong>: Biology, Context, Market and Survival.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Biology: are you comfortable with uncertain income?</div>
        <p>Calculate your twelve-month personal costs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Context: time, money and home support</div>
        <p>Count study time, fees and support at home.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Market: who hires?</div>
        <p>Read ten notices for these roles and note the common skills.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Survival: what survives AI?</div>
        <p>Routine reporting shrinks. Judgment and ownership hold value.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gate3">The 3 Gates: proof before commitment</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>The 3 Gates</strong> check that your effort turns into work other people rely on.
  </p>
  <div class="gates-block">
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of demand</span>
        <p>Share interview notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of sales</span>
        <p>Show payments.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of numbers</span>
        <p>Share a unit view.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Expensive mistakes</h2>

  <div class="mistake-list">
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Building before talking to customers</div>
        <p>Interview first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Borrowing early</div>
        <p>Test cheaply.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Ignoring runway</div>
        <p>Calculate it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Ignoring your own time cost</div>
        <p>Include it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Seeking funding before sales</div>
        <p>Get customers first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Pick one route, finish one project and show it to two people in the field. Then read ten live notices and apply or pitch a small client.
  </p>
  <p>
    A specialist can look at your strengths, finances and goals with you. A sensible first step is <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/student-career-guidance/">student career guidance</a>. The aim is a high-income skill portfolio and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>

  <p>
    For what to compare and a four-week plan, read <a href="/blog/college-degrees/bms-vs-bba-which-to-choose-india/">BMS vs BBA</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQs on MBA entrepreneurship</h2>

  <div class="faq-accordion">
